\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Use case diagram: actors, use cases, and \texttt {<<include>>}/\texttt {<<uses>>} relationships across the five layers.}}{17}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Class diagram: agent hierarchy, debate data classes, and RL environment/policy classes.}}{18}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Sequence diagram: one hourly decision cycle, from a new OHLCV bar to a placed paper order and dispatched alert.}}{19}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces Deployment diagram: Docker containers, mounted volumes, the host-process LLM, and external service dependencies.}}{20}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.5}{\ignorespaces Contrastive pretraining of the regime encoder: two augmented views of the same window are encoded with shared weights and pulled together in embedding space, while other windows in the mini-batch act as negatives pushed apart by the NT-Xent loss.}}{23}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.6}{\ignorespaces Regime detection pipeline: engineered features $\to $ BIC-guided state-count search $\to $ best-of-5-seed Gaussian HMM fit $\to $ regime probability stream, consumed by Layers 3 and 4.}}{26}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Multi-agent deliberation flow: Round 1 (three LLM directional agents plus the deterministic Risk agent), the conditional Contrarian check and Round 2 rebuttals, and the deterministic Fund Manager synthesis producing the final decision.}}{31}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.8}{\ignorespaces RL execution agent: the shared policy trunk feeds a Categorical direction head and a Beta position-fraction head, whose combined output is executed by the environment and scored by the CVaR-normalized reward, producing the next observation.}}{33}{}%
