\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Per-regime historical Sharpe (bars, left axis) and annualized volatility (line, right axis), six-state five-asset 22-column configuration. Time-share annotations below each bar show the fraction of pooled 2018--2025 hours spent in that regime.}}{45}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Absolute Sharpe ratio per ablation row against the buy-and-hold reference (dashed line, Sharpe 1.498). Error bars show the 95\% block-bootstrap confidence interval on the Sharpe delta, re-centered onto the absolute Sharpe axis; bar color follows the significance verdict of Table~\ref {tab:rl-ablation-crypto5}.}}{51}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces BTC-only weekly-cadence grid: the pre-registered checkpoint's $\Delta $ Sharpe vs.\ buy-hold on 2024 validation (blue) against the same checkpoint's $\Delta $ on 2025 test (red/green), from Table~\ref {tab:rl-weekly-2025}. Diamonds show the individual-seed 2024 $\Delta $ values of Table~\ref {tab:rl-weekly-grid} as context for the spread the pre-registered checkpoint was drawn from. Conditions A and B flip sign between the two years; C and D do not.}}{53}{}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Crypto5 panel extension, 2025-only $\Delta $ Sharpe vs.\ buy-hold per asset and condition (Table~\ref {tab:rl-weekly-crypto5-2025}). ETH is the one asset where all four conditions, including both the real regime condition (C) and its noise control (D), lose to buy-hold.}}{55}{}%
